==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|attritio||a rubbing against|lang=la}}, from the verb {{term|attritus|lang=la}}, past participle of {{term|atterere||to wear|lang=la}}, from {{term|ad-||to, towards|lang=la}} + {{term|terere||to rub|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[əˈtɹɪʃən]|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɪʃən|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# wearing or grinding down by [[friction]].
# the [[gradual]] reduction in a tangible or intangible resource due to causes that are passive and do not involve productive use of the resource.
# {{context|human resources|lang=en}} A gradual, natural reduction in [[membership]] or [[personnel]], as through retirement, resignation, or [[death]].
# {{context|sciences|lang=en}} The loss of [[participant]]s during an [[experiment]].
# {{context|theology|lang=en}} Imperfect [[contrition]] or remorse.
# {{context|dentistry|lang=en}} The wearing of teeth due to their grinding.

